Subject: [PATCH] ipconfig: don't sleep 10 ms for a static address

ip_auto_config() sleeps CONF_POST_OPEN (10 ms, two jiffies at HZ=100)
after opening the devices, to "give drivers a chance to settle" before
BOOTP/DHCP/RARP talk through them. With a complete static configuration
on a single device (ip=ADDR::GW:MASK::DEV:off) nothing is sent, so the
sleep only delays boot: on microvm it would be ten times the whole boot.

--- a/net/ipv4/ipconfig.c	2026-11-04 19:18:08.272655097 +0100
+++ b/net/ipv4/ipconfig.c	2026-11-04 19:18:08.288697761 +0100
@@ -1517,8 +1517,11 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	/* Give drivers a chance to settle */
-	msleep(CONF_POST_OPEN);
+	/* Give drivers a chance to settle, unless nothing will be asked of
+	 * them: a static address on the only device.
+	 */
+	if (ic_myaddr == NONE || ic_first_dev->next)
+		msleep(CONF_POST_OPEN);
 
 	/*
 	 * If the config information is insufficient (e.g., our IP address or
